# Trained artifacts, regenerated by any run of the script.
# Pickled sklearn objects are version-brittle -- a .joblib saved by one
# scikit-learn release often refuses to load in another -- so committing
# them would ship a file that breaks on someone else's machine. Training
# takes under a second; just retrain.
spam_model.joblib
vectorizer.joblib
*.joblib

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store

# Test artefacts. .coverage is a binary database of one local run, so it
# changes on every invocation and shows as a modified file forever. It was
# committed here by accident -- the transit project in this family had the
# same one and its .gitignore says so.
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# The optional sentence encoder. ~88 MB of weights, fetched with the curl
# commands in requirements-embeddings.txt. Not committed for the same reason
# the .joblib artifacts are not: a binary blob in git history that most
# clones will never load, and GitHub would reject it over the 100 MB limit
# soon enough anyway.
models/
